RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE

Office of City Clerk

February 25, 2020

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date
beginning at 6:00p.m. in City Council Chambers for the purpose of collective labor bargaining
with the Cheyenne Professional Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local
No. 279.  Present were:  MAYOR - Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS – Bryan Cook, Ken
Esquibel, Mike Luna, Dr. Mark Rinne, Scott Roybal and Dicky Shanor.  Absent:  Rocky Case,
Pete Laybourn and Jeff White.  Also present: Kylie Soden, Deputy City Clerk; Michael O’Donnell,
City Attorney; Alessandra McCoy-Fakelman, Deputy City Attorney and Robin Lockman, City
Treasurer.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Mayor Orr requested those who may be speaking to use the microphones so that their
comments can be heard.  Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded and available
on Facebook live and stated that Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings
Act allows the governing body to meet in executive session to consider or tender offers regarding
salaries, wages or other terms and conditions of employment during negotiations with the fire
fighters union and that any motion approved by the governing body to move into executive session
during the special meetings would be pursuant to this section of statute.  Mayor Orr further advised
if the governing body met in executive session, they would be meeting in the Mayor’s Conference
Room, and that Fire Union representatives were welcome to use Committee Room 104 for the
purpose of meeting to caucus.

Mayor Orr advised the last meeting resulted in mutual agreement of several sections in the
City’s initial offer. TJ Haws, Union representative, presented their proposal, explained the format
and inquired as to the review process.  Discussion continued on the desired format of offers to be
presented moving forward.

Pursuant to Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x), Mr. Shanor moved to meet in
executive session, seconded by Mr. Luna.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body present.  Mayor Orr identified, in addition to members of the governing body
present, the Deputy City Clerk, City Attorney, Deputy City Attorney and City Treasurer would
also be present at the executive session.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the special meeting
was stopped; executive Session convened at 6:11 p.m. in the Mayor’s Conference Room]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at
7:22 p.m.  Discussion followed on the process of exchanging and presenting offers at future
meetings.  Mayor Orr advised the City rejected the Union’s proposed offers for the following
Sections and counter-offered with the City’s original proposed offers for each section: Section 2-
Definitions, Section 3-Exclusive Bargaining Agent, Section 8-Grievance Procedures, Section 13-
Management Rights, Section 15-Department Staffing, Section 17-Hours of Work, Section 18-
Trading Shifts, Section 19-Inclement Weather Conditions, Section 20-Holidays, Section 22-
```

