Overtime, Section 23-Working in a Higher Job Rank, Section 24-Specialized Emergency
Response Teams, Section 25-Conversion of Benefit Hours, Section 26-Wellness/Fitness Program,
Section 28-Sick Leave, Section 35-Mileage Allowance and Section 37-Time Off for Union
Business.  Mayor Orr advised the City accepted the Union’s proposed offers for Section 12-Union
Representation and Section 34-Union Dues.  Section 21-Classification of Employment and Basic
Wages and Section 41-Prevailing Rights were presented with counter offers and explained to the
Union. Union proposed Section 46-Milary Leave, Section 47-Tuition Reimbursement and Section
48-Parental Leave were rejected by the City.  Union representatives asked for detailed clarification
and provided information related to their proposals on the following Sections: Section 2-
Definitions, Section 3-Exclusive Bargaining Agreement, Section 8-Grievance Procedures, Section
13-Management Rights, Section 15-Department Staffing, Section 17-Hours of Work, Section 18-
Trading Shifts, Section 19-Inclement Weather Conditions, Section 20-Holidays, Section 21-
Classification of Employment and Basic Wages, Section 22-Overtime, Section 24-Specialized
Emergency Response Teams, Section 25-Conversion of Benefit Hours, Section 26-
Wellness/Fitness Program, Section 28-Sick Leave, Section 35-Mileage Allowance, Section 37-
Time Off for Union Business, Section 41-Prevailing Rights, Section 46-Military Leave, Section
47-Tuition Reimbursement and Section 48-Parental Leave.

Mayor Orr stated the purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no other
business previously noted for the special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 8:27 p.m.

Submitted by,

Kylie Soden,

Deputy City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.

Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

March 6, 2020
